Across the city the pattern holds. Of Philadelphia's 384 tracts in 2006-2010, just 6 produce a white poverty rate that meets the standard threshold for reliability: 1.6% of the city. Another 189 tracts, 49.2%, are unreliable outright, and 10 more yield no rate at all. The article builds several of its sharpest claims on a measure that works in six tracts out of 384.

